# Browser profiles hold live logged-in sessions — never commit them.
profiles/
# Failure dumps can contain page content from a logged-in session.
artifacts/
# Local job journal, staged uploads and generated decks — machine state, not
# source. The PDFs in outputs/ are rebuilt from a job at any time.
jobs.json
uploads/
outputs/
bridge.log
__pycache__/
# Run lock — live process state, not source. Guards against two deck runs
# overlapping, which creates two notebooks and spends twice the quota.
.deck-run.lock
.deck-run.test.lock
.reels-run.lock
# NOTE: there is no local reels file any more. The harvest POSTs to Veda's
# Worker (V1/workers/studyos-api /reels) and the cloud is the only store, so
# nothing reel-shaped lands on disk to ignore. Kept as a reminder not to
# reintroduce one: a local copy would be a second source of truth that only
# this machine can see, and the phone is the whole point.
